.TH MDT.RECOVERY_HISTOGRAM 4 2026-08-23 Lustre "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
recovery_histogram \- per-phase client delay histograms per recovery
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.BI "lctl get_param mdt." TARGET ".recovery_histogram"
.SY
.BI "lctl get_param obdfilter." TARGET ".recovery_histogram"
.SY
.BI "lctl set_param mdt." TARGET ".recovery_histogram=clear"
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Access Permissions
.BR 644 " | " -rw-r--r--
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Per MDT or OST target device
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B recovery_histogram
parameter reports a log2-bucketed histogram for each of the three recovery
phases (reconnect, req_replay, lock_replay). Each histogram counts how many
seconds each client spent inside that phase alone: the reconnect histogram
measures from the start of the recovery window, and each replay histogram
measures from the later of two points: when that client finished the
preceding phase, and when the recovery thread entered this phase. Because
each phase is a barrier, a client that finishes early waits for the slowest
client, and that wait belongs to the phase's start rather than to the client.
A client that never reached the preceding phase is counted from the start of
the recovery window instead. The histogram is reset when recovery begins, so
it always reflects the most recent recovery. Writing any value to the
parameter clears all three phases.
.PP
In contrast,
.BR mdt.recovery_top (4)
ranks clients by their cumulative offset from the start of recovery (i.e. by
when they finished, not by how long the phase took them), and
.BR mdt.recovery_delay (4)
reports the three cumulative offsets for a single client export.
.PP
Output is YAML. Leading scalars report the recovery window
.RB ( recovery_start ", " req_replay_start ", " lock_replay_start ", "
.RB recovery_finish ", " recovery_time " in seconds),"
and each phase then contributes a
.BI <phase> _delay_seconds_samples
count followed by a
.BI client_ <phase> _histogram
list, where <phase> is one of reconnect, req_replay or lock_replay.
Each list entry reports a bucket upper bound
.RB ( phase_sec ),
the number of clients whose duration for that phase fell into that bucket
.RB ( clients ),
that bucket's percentage of the total
.RB ( pct ),
and the cumulative percentage
.RB ( cum_pct ).
Buckets that no client fell into are omitted entirely, so the list only
contains buckets with at least one client.
.PP
Per-client
.BR mdt.recovery_delay (4)
parameters are also exposed individually under each client mountpoint's
.BI mdt. TARGET .exports. NID .recovery_delay
and
.BI obdfilter. TARGET .exports. NID .recovery_delay
parameter. This is useful for isolating a specific client's recovery delay,
which is otherwise shown in aggregate form in the full histogram,
or may not be in the
.BR mdt.recovery_top (4)
list.
.SH MODULES
This parameter is in the following modules:
.EX
.B mdt.*.recovery_histogram
.B obdfilter.*.recovery_histogram
.EE
.SH EXAMPLES
Show the histogram for an MDT after a recovery:
.EX
.RB mds# " lctl get_param -n mdt.lfs-MDT0000.recovery_histogram"
recovery_start:    1780002682
req_replay_start:  1780002700
lock_replay_start: 1780002714
recovery_finish:   1780002729
recovery_time:     47
reconnect_delay_seconds_samples: 58
client_reconnect_histogram:
- { phase_sec:   1, clients:   45, pct:  77, cum_pct:  77 }
- { phase_sec:   2, clients:    6, pct:  10, cum_pct:  87 }
- { phase_sec:   4, clients:    4, pct:   7, cum_pct:  94 }
- { phase_sec:   8, clients:    2, pct:   3, cum_pct:  97 }
- { phase_sec:  32, clients:    1, pct:   3, cum_pct: 100 }
req_replay_delay_seconds_samples: 58
client_req_replay_histogram:
- { phase_sec:   1, clients:   57, pct:  98, cum_pct:  98 }
- { phase_sec:   2, clients:    1, pct:   2, cum_pct: 100 }
lock_replay_delay_seconds_samples: 58
client_lock_replay_histogram:
- { phase_sec:   1, clients:   58, pct: 100, cum_pct: 100 }
.EE
Clear the histogram:
.EX
.RB mds# " lctl set_param mdt.lfs-MDT0000.recovery_histogram=clear"
.EE
Writing any value clears every phase.
.SH AVAILABILITY
.B recovery_histogram
is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.18.0.
.\" commit v2_17_53
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mdt.recovery_delay (4),
.BR mdt.recovery_top (4),
.BR lctl-get_param (8),
.BR lctl-set_param (8)
